{
  "title": "Thumb Hypoplasia",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/hand/6083/thumb-hypoplasia",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jan 17 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Thumb hypoplasia is the congenital underdevelopment of the thumb frequently associated with partial or complete absence of the radius.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with hypoplasia of the thumb and thenar musculature. Radiographs help determine musculotendinous versus osseous deficiencies.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment may be observation, soft tissue reconstruction, pollicization, or amputation depending on the level of the deficit and presence of carpometacarpal joint instability.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "1/100,000 live births",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "male = female",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic location",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**bilateral involvement** in ~60% of patients",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "right hand more common than left",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "exact cause during embryologic development has yet to be elucidated",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "likely due to abnormalities involving the AER, progress zone, and FGF signaling molecules",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated anomalies",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "greater than **80% of patients will have associated anomalies** including",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "VACTERL",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Holt-Oram",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "thrombocytopenia-absent radius (TAR)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Fanconi anemia",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Cornelia de Lange syndrome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "Okihiro syndrome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
